+/*
+ * (raphael, 2026-11-07) The window server's vsync kept on when it asks for it off (boot-arg sweetfb_vsynckeep,
+ * kern.sweet_fb_vsync_keep). CoreAnimation turns its vsync notifications off whenever nothing is due and on
+ * again when a commit comes (~4500 times in a bench): in a program-driven animation (the home page settling
+ * after a swipe) that was every frame, and each time the frame came two refreshes late -- shown three
+ * refreshes (37 ms) where MIUI's 60 Hz shows every one. Kept on, the next tick is there when the commit is.
+ */
+extern "C" uint32_t sweet_fb_vsync_keep;
